1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Three teammates. One Session. One agent.
The task: plan a better bug-report product.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Join the conversation at any time.
Maya drafts a message. Eli and Sam see that she’s typing.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
One live browser, shared by the team.
Eli clicks “Review together” on the concept page.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
The same live page, in three clients.
These are three different clients viewing the same live browser.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Capture the page before adding feedback.
Annotations stay with this version, even if the live browser moves on.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Maya pins a design concern.
“Lead with shared evidence, not blame.”

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Eli replies to Maya’s note.
First release: capture runtime versions and the failing command.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Sam marks a region and raises an edge case.
For the product under review: what should happen offline?

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,000
One discussion, visible to everyone.
The same note and reply appear in each client, with names and colors intact.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:10,000
The same agent receives the image and feedback.
The team’s comments become context for the continuing conversation.

11
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
“Works on our machines.”
One shared Session. Everyone can contribute. The agent keeps the context.
